  "narration": {
    "title": "The Bats Take Over: Alvarez Leads a Loud Week",
    "intro": "The hitters get the floor today. Yordan Alvarez is still the best bat in the game, and a wave of sluggers just spent the week padding their home run totals. The season leaderboards, meanwhile, have a few names you might not expect.",
    "offense_lead": "The Dodgers pace the team-OPS board at .785, a step clear of the Pirates at .766. Washington and Colorado sit right behind, a reminder that a modest record doesn't always mean a quiet lineup.",
    "bats_lead": "Alvarez holds the top of the elite hitters list at a 1.041 OPS and 29 homers, three of them against Tampa Bay over a July weekend. Juan Soto is the one climbing, up to .985 with three homers off Atlanta and Kansas City, while James Wood jumped fifty points on the week to .949.",
    "season_leaders_lead": "Kyle Schwarber leads the home run race at 31, with Alvarez right behind at 29. Jordan Walker tops the RBI list at 69, and Otto Lopez quietly owns the batting title at .343.",
    "hr_lead": "James Wood and Matt Olson each added four homers this week to lead the climbers, Wood pairing a night against Pittsburgh with back-to-back shots off Houston and Olson taking a pair off the Mets twice over. Alvarez, Soto and Ben Rice each chipped in three."
  }
